WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.778 --> 00:00:14.620
When the minister saw Tom walking forward to receive the Bible, he was shocked.

2
00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:19.403
The minister could not imagine how Tom had mastered two thousand lines of verse.

3
00:00:20.484 --> 00:00:22.145
But the boys and girls sitting there knew.

4
00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:25.588
They had sold their tickets for the sake of Tom's glory.

5
00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:31.912
After Tom received his Bible, he was introduced to the judge, the new girl's father.

6
00:00:32.776 --> 00:00:33.577
"What's your name?"

7
00:00:33.977 --> 00:00:34.657
asked the judge.

8
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:40.260
stuttered a very nervous Tom.

9
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:45.163
"You're a fine boy, Thomas, and two thousand verses is a lot of verses.

10
00:00:46.343 --> 00:00:48.665
You won't be sorry you learned them," said the judge.

11
00:00:50.085 --> 00:00:54.368
Tom thought he was free to go, but then the judge continued, "Knowledge is precious.

12
00:00:55.108 --> 00:00:58.650
It's what makes good men great, and I can see you'll be a great man.

13
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.646
I'm sure you know the names of all of Jesus' disciples, but who were his first two disciples?"

14
00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:09.330
Tom was uncertain if he was supposed to answer, so he remained quiet.

15
00:01:09.351 --> 00:01:13.895
"Thomas, answer the question," the minister prodded him.

16
00:01:14.796 --> 00:01:20.041
At that, Tom shouted out the only two names from the Bible he could remember, "David and Goliath!"

17
00:01:20.902 --> 00:01:22.663
The church erupted into laughter.

18
00:01:23.404 --> 00:01:24.865
Tom slunk back to his seat.

19
00:01:25.686 --> 00:01:27.188
His aunt poked him angrily.

20
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.583
The next morning Tom woke up knowing it was Monday, and Monday meant school.

21
00:01:35.623 --> 00:01:39.386
Tom hated school more than he hated work, and this Monday was no different.

22
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:43.769
He was feeling especially sheepish after his fall from grace at the church.

23
00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:46.791
But at school he would see the new girl.

24
00:01:47.811 --> 00:01:48.872
School would be bearable.

25
00:01:51.614 --> 00:01:53.615
On the way to school, Tom met his friend Huck.

26
00:01:54.976 --> 00:01:59.219
Huck's father was a drunk, so Huck was the only boy in town who didn't have to go

27
00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:00.380
to church or school.

28
00:02:01.216 --> 00:02:02.998
"Hey, Huck," said Tom.

29
00:02:03.718 --> 00:02:05.700
He noticed that his friend was holding something.

30
00:02:06.561 --> 00:02:07.481
"What have you got?"

31
00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:10.604
"Something that will cure warts," said Huck.

32
00:02:10.624 --> 00:02:14.407
"I have lots of warts," said Tom.

33
00:02:14.427 --> 00:02:19.111
"Come with me to the graveyard tonight, and I can get rid of them for you," said Huck.

34
00:02:20.032 --> 00:02:21.473
Tom thought that was a good idea.

35
00:02:22.454 --> 00:02:25.616
Tom and Huck said good-bye, and Tom continued walking to school.

36
00:02:27.178 --> 00:02:29.780
By the time Tom finally got to school, he was late.

37
00:02:31.688 --> 00:02:32.589
"Where have you been?"

38
00:02:33.029 --> 00:02:33.870
the teacher asked.

39
00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.693
Tom usually made up a story when he was late.

40
00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:39.695
But today was different.

41
00:02:41.377 --> 00:02:45.180
If he told the teacher the truth, he would be punished by being made to sit with the

42
00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.784
girls. He saw that the only empty seat was beside the new girl.

43
00:02:50.424 --> 00:02:52.406
His punishment would be to sit next to her!

44
00:02:52.426 --> 00:02:56.550
"I was talking with Huckleberry Finn," answered Tom.

45
00:02:57.871 --> 00:02:59.012
The teacher was shocked.

46
00:02:59.976 --> 00:03:00.677
"Thomas Sawyer!

47
00:03:00.977 --> 00:03:04.059
That boy is bad, and you should not talk with bad boys."

48
00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.023
Tom apologized, and the teacher made him sit next to the new girl.

49
00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:12.807
Tom saw the winks and heard the whispers of the other boys and girls, but he didn't care.

50
00:03:13.707 --> 00:03:16.650
He was happy that his plan had worked, and he pretended to read.

51
00:03:17.691 --> 00:03:19.512
Tom put a peach on the new girl's desk.

52
00:03:20.773 --> 00:03:24.036
Tom then wrote on his slate, "Please take it.

53
00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:24.917
I have more."

54
00:03:26.598 --> 00:03:28.680
The girl read the slate and quickly looked away.

55
00:03:30.532 --> 00:03:34.454
Soon Tom began to draw, and with his left hand, he hid what he was drawing.

56
00:03:34.474 --> 00:03:38.655
"Let me see," the girl whispered.

57
00:03:38.676 --> 00:03:43.798
"I wish I could draw," she said when Tom finally showed her.

58
00:03:43.818 --> 00:03:46.839
"It's easy," said Tom.

59
00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.280
"Stay for lunch and I'll teach you.

60
00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.021
What's your name?"

61
00:03:51.041 --> 00:03:52.941
"I'm Becky Thatcher.

62
00:03:53.402 --> 00:03:55.322
What's your Oh, I know.

63
00:03:55.923 --> 00:03:57.203
I remember you from church.

64
00:03:57.823 --> 00:03:58.824
You're Thomas Sawyer."

65
00:03:59.596 --> 00:04:02.617
"They only call me that when I'm bad," said Tom.

66
00:04:03.578 --> 00:04:04.978
"You can call me Tom."

67
00:04:06.059 --> 00:04:09.500
Tom wrote some words on his slate, and again he hid them from Becky.

68
00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.301
She begged to see them.

69
00:04:11.981 --> 00:04:14.642
Tom whispered: "Promise you won't tell."

70
00:04:15.283 --> 00:04:17.223
"I promise," said Becky.

71
00:04:18.064 --> 00:04:21.345
Tom moved his hand, and Becky read the words: "'I love you.'

72
00:04:21.925 --> 00:04:22.946
Oh, you're bad!"

73
00:04:23.786 --> 00:04:28.428
She blushed and turned away, but Tom saw her smiling, and he knew she was pleased.

74
00:04:30.672 --> 00:04:34.975
At lunch Tom and Becky met behind the schoolhouse, and Tom asked Becky a question.

75
00:04:35.876 --> 00:04:37.457
"Have you ever been engaged?"

76
00:04:38.497 --> 00:04:40.159
"No," replied Becky.

77
00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.980
"Would you like to be?"

78
00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:42.940
asked Tom.

79
00:04:43.881 --> 00:04:46.003
"Maybe. What's special about it?"

80
00:04:47.504 --> 00:04:53.848
"Well," said Tom, "first we kiss, and then you only like me, and I only like you.

81
00:04:54.448 --> 00:04:56.630
And we walk to and from school together."

82
00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:01.938
Becky thought it sounded nice, so she said, "I love you," in Tom's ear.

83
00:05:01.958 --> 00:05:06.081
"I never thought I'd be engaged," said Becky smiling.

84
00:05:06.101 --> 00:05:08.703
"It's fun," said Tom.

85
00:05:08.723 --> 00:05:14.127
"Amy and I—" "Oh, Tom, you've been engaged before!"

86
00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.992
shouted Becky, and she began to cry.

87
00:05:21.013 --> 00:05:23.575
Tom tried to comfort her, but she wouldn't listen.

88
00:05:24.135 --> 00:05:25.456
She was hurt and angry.

89
00:05:25.476 --> 00:05:27.618
"I only care for you!"

90
00:05:28.079 --> 00:05:29.600
said Tom, and he left.
